OL,3,CHow and when to watch the solar
OL,4,Ceclipse in the North East and North
OL,5,CYorkshire
OL,7,FPeople across the North East and North
OL,8,FYorkshire will likely be looking to
OL,9,Fthe skies this evening as the world
OL,10,Fbraces for a once-in-a-generation
OL,11,Fsolar eclipse.
OL,13,FMore than 90% of the sun will be
OL,14,Fobscured by the moon between about 6pm
OL,15,Fand 8.15pm on Wednesday (12 August) -
OL,16,Fthat's the most it has been blocked
OL,17,Ffor those in the UK since the total
OL,18,Feclipse in 1999.
OL,1,W~k4~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}        G1/7
